Upcasting and Downcasting of Polymorphism
Upcasting- From Child To Parent Class.
Downcastig-From Parent to Child Class.(Direct downcasting is not possible in java).

Non primitive typeCasting:
-The process of Converting the reference from one non-primitive type to another non-primitive tye is called non-primitive.
-In this we have 2 types:
1.Auto Upcasting - The process of convertig the reference frm child type to parent type.
                   This process is Automatic frm JDK 1.5 version so it is called as Auto Upcasting.
                   Whenever we performupcasting we can access only parent class.
2.Explicit Downcasting - Converting a parent class reference into a child class reference is called explicit downcasting.
                       - And the process is not automatic so we have to perform explicitly by using typecast opoerator , 
                         hence it is called as Explicit Downcasting.
                       - Whenever we try to perform direct downcasting we will get class cast exception because the 
                         members of sub class are not present in the object created.
